	(text "1. OFF-BOARD SOURCE: T1 (2 x 18 V AC, 30 VA) and both secondary fuses FSEC1/FSEC2 are off this PCB.\n   Mains primary, inlet, primary fuse, switch and PE bonding stay in the enclosure; none of it reaches this board.\n   Phase the windings so A2-B1 gives ~36 V AC between J1.1 and J1.4; check before connecting the bridge.\n\n2. SOURCE SELECTION: J2 (NORMAL_SOURCE) reaches J3 (SYSTEM_FEED) ONLY through the removable pin-for-pin cable.\n   There must be NO copper, jumper or shared ground joining REG_* / PSU_0V to SYS_* / SYS_0V on this PCB.\n   Bench mode: remove that cable and feed J3 (+15 V, 0 V, -15 V, +7.5 V). Swap plugs only with sources off and discharged.\n\n3. HEATSINKS: TO-220 tabs are at different potentials: U1 = REG_P15, U3 = REG_AUX, U2 = RAW_N (about -25 V).\n   Each regulator needs an insulating pad and shoulder washer; tabs must not share bare metal or touch the case.\n   Preliminary target: <= 10 C/W per sink; about 3.9 W each for U1/U2 and 3.1 W for U3 at the 33 V raw ceiling.\n\n4. STATUS INTERFACE (J6): do NOT tie STATUS_0V to SYS_0V or PSU_0V on this board.\n   The converter must fit a 47k pulldown on PSU_VALID at its receiver, use a 3.3 V Schmitt input,\n   require 100 ms continuously valid before arming, and latch any rail-loss fault until explicit re-arm.\n\n5. CHASSIS (J7): no PSU_0V / SYS_0V / STATUS_0V to chassis link by default; the single signal-to-chassis bond is set at system level.\n\n6. STORED ENERGY: C1 and C2 each hold about 2.5 J at 33 V. The bleeders alone need about 90 s to reach 5 V; measure before touching.\n   Never clip an earthed scope ground to RAW_N or SYS_N15.\n\n7. BOM: resistor tolerance/power and capacitor voltage are part of each part's fields (MPN, LCSC, Tolerance, Power, Voltage).\n   R2/R4 must be 0.25 W. C7 must be wet aluminium. TP1-TP10 and J7 are copper only (excluded from BOM)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
